{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124055","id":4700851247,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGDFMLw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124055/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124055/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f6adfeded58dc6b16587507a92b5924220883cac","number":124055,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Optimize `Object::get_script` and refactor internal usage to avoid Refs","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Optimize `Object::get_script()`\r\n- Code style/performance improvement to call-sites of `Object::get_script()`\r\n- Follow up to #123810\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`Object::get_script` currently has an extra set of ref/unref. When used as a temporary, this is a total of two pairs of refs and unrefs.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/084a2caa05119b625a99b6b51d44b459a26362de/core/object/object.cpp#L1089-L1091\r\n\r\nInstead of constructing a temporary `Ref` and then using `Ref::operator Variant()`, we use the `Variant(const Object *)` constructor which still increments ref count.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nVariant Object::get_script() const {\r\n-\treturn script_instance ? Variant(Ref<Script>(script_instance->get_script())) : Variant();\r\n+ \treturn script_instance ? Variant(script_instance->get_script()) : Variant();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nYet even with these changes the following common pattern still results in two pairs of ref/unrefs. One for the Variant temporary and one for the local Ref variable. \r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nRef<Script> script = obj->get_script();\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith #123810, the above pattern can already be done with no refs.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nScript *script = obj->get_script_instance() != nullptr ? obj->get_script_instance()->get_script() : nullptr;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe above snippet is the new `Object::get_script()` as this is used extensively internally. The old Variant version is binded as a new function.\r\n\r\nThis PR updates about two-thirds of call-sites of `Object::get_script()` to not use a Ref. The remaining third has been changed to call the new optimized `Object::get_script_bind()` instead (same functionality as the old `get_script`).\r\n\r\n## Organization of Changes\r\n\r\nStarting with the Object API changes:\r\n\r\n* `core/object/object.h`\r\n* `core/object/object.cpp`\r\n\r\nThe changes from #123810 have been updated to use the new helper\r\n\r\n* `core/variant/container_type_validate.cpp`\r\n* `modules/gdscript/gdscript_function.cpp`\r\n\r\nThe rest are a blanket update of `get_script` calls that do not need a Ref. The ones that cannot change to the `Script *` version have been updated to call the bind version instead.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Code</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nclass_name A extends Object\r\n\r\nvar x: A\r\n```\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _on_json_button_pressed() -> void:\r\n\tvar a : Array\r\n\t\r\n\tfor i in 20:\r\n\t\ta.push_back(A.new())\r\n\t\r\n\tvar start = Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n\t\r\n\tfor i in 50_000:\r\n\t\tJSON.from_native(a, true)\r\n\t\r\n\tprint(Time.get_ticks_msec() - start)\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _on_get_script_button_pressed() -> void:\r\n\tvar a = A.new()\r\n\t\r\n\tvar start = Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n\t\r\n\tfor i in 10_000_000:\r\n\t\ta.get_script()\r\n\t\r\n\tprint(Time.get_ticks_msec() - start)\r\n```\r\n\r\nNote: the JSON benchmark is normalized per object in the array. Calculated as t / 20 / 50,000 * 10e9.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nRun 21 times on release templates and 10th percentile is summarized below.\r\n\r\n| Function | Master (ns/op) | PR (ns/op) | Diff | Speedup |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| JSON.from_native() | 840 | 773 | 67 | 1.09x |\r\n| Object.get_script() | 62.5 | 45.4 | 17.1 | 1.38x |\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels